vibeos (1:0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release of VibeOS, the new name of gnome-phone: a GNOME-based
    system for touch devices (phones and tablets now; desktops with touch
    and TV boxes to come). It carries on from gnome-phone 0.1.11; the
    history of gnome-phone's releases is in git.
  * Everything is renamed: the packages (gnome-phone-* and neo-* are
    vibeos-*, libneo is libvibeos, fonts-neo-roboto is fonts-vibeos-roboto),
    the programs, desktop ids, D-Bus names and GSettings schemas (neo.* are
    vibeos.*, neo.Phone is vibeos.Shell), the extension (gnome-phone@neo is
    shell@vibeos), the session (gnome-phone is vibeos), the font family
    (VibeOS Roboto) and the per-user directories.
  * Upgrading from gnome-phone: the vibeos packages replace the old ones
    (Conflicts/Replaces/Provides). The app packages save each user's home
    layout before the old launcher can rearrange it, vibeos-session moves the
    users' login session and a mobile shell's unit drop-in over to vibeos,
    and vibeos-migrate-ids carries each user's settings, files, shortcuts and
    home screen over at the next login.
  * Icon packs: VibeOS, the new default (large glyphs on squircles in each
    app's colour), and gnome-free (gnome-phone's Round pack, renamed).
  * Packaging: an upgrade no longer stops the session's units (the phone's
    session is the whole UI); input-boost restarts after an upgrade.
  * The version has an epoch (1:): sim-apn and the libspongy packages keep
    their names, and 1:0.1.0 follows gnome-phone's 0.1.11 for them.

 -- pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:53:04 +0100
